Found during k147 live wire probing. Role::ResponsesCompatible::_responses_extra_fields lifts the output[] search_results block into Response.citations, but it is only called from chat_response (non-streaming). parse_stream_chunk / the stream aggregation never extract search_results, so a STREAMED search-augmented Perplexity reply loses its citations. Live evidence: non-streaming probe A returned 10 citations; the streaming envelope carries search_results in output[] frames / the response.completed payload but the parser ignores them. Shared behavior with Engine::OpenAIResponses (same role), though only Perplexity currently streams. Fix: surface citations on the streaming path (e.g. lift search_results in parse_stream_chunk into Stream::Chunk, or from the final response.completed output[] during aggregation). Out of scope for the k147 8-point confirmation.

